title: Vesting incentive for validator self-stake

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Enable vested incentive payouts for validator self-stake (issue #11876) instead of the
    previous immediate (liquid) transfers.

    ## Changes to `pallet-vesting`:

    - New `VestedPayout` trait method: `add_to_vesting(source, dest, amount, duration, start_at)`
      - If a vesting schedule that starts at `start_at` exists, it is merged with this schedule
      - Otherwise, we attempt to create a new vesting schedule with the given arguments
    - Two corresponding new `WeightInfo` methods: `add_to_vesting_create` and `add_to_vesting_merge`.

    ## Changes to `pallet-staking-async`:

    - New `#[pallet::no_default]` `Config` items:
      - `VestingBondingPeriods`: Number of bonding-duration windows to vest over (`0` = liquid).
      - `BlocksPerSession`: The number of blocks in a session.
      - `VestingBlockNumberProvider`: Block-number provider matching pallet-vesting's clock.
      - `ValidatorIncentivePayout`: Payout adapter trait with 2 implementations: `LiquidIncentivePayout`
          or `VestedIncentivePayout`.

    - The `VestingEpochStart` storage item tracks the start of the current vesting window; it is
      seeded on the first era after the runtime upgrade, so that vesting can begin immediately.
      If delivery fails for any reason, the incentive is dropped (no liquid fallback).

crates:
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: major
- name: pallet-vesting
  bump: major
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
